{"version": 2, "width": 100, "height": 32, "title": "etp-custody \u2014 end-to-end demo", "env": {"TERM": "xterm-256color", "SHELL": "/bin/bash"}}
[0.18, "o", "\r\n"]
[1.28, "o", "\u001b[1;36m\u25b8 1. Generate keys \u2014 a notary operator, a recipient (Bob), a capturing device\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.46, "o", "\u2713 wrote keypair \u2192 operator.key  (label=notary)\r\n"]
[1.64, "o", "\u2713 wrote keypair \u2192 bob.key  (label=bob)\r\n"]
[1.82, "o", "\u2713 wrote public key \u2192 bob.pub  (shareable)\r\n"]
[2.0, "o", "\u2713 wrote keypair \u2192 sensor7.key  (label=sensor7)\r\n"]
[2.18, "o", "\u2713 wrote public key \u2192 sensor7.pub  (shareable)\r\n"]
[2.36, "o", "\r\n"]
[3.46, "o", "\u001b[1;36m\u25b8 2. Stand up the notary (append-only Merkle log)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.64, "o", "\u2713 initialized notary at ./notary\r\n"]
[3.82, "o", "\r\n"]
[4.92, "o", "\u001b[1;36m\u25b8 3. Create a confidential artifact\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[5.1, "o", "    TOP SECRET \u2014 quarterly telemetry, confidential through 2045\r\n"]
[5.28, "o", "\r\n"]
[6.38, "o", "\u001b[1;36m\u25b8 4. send: seal (PQC) + notarize + device-sign + erasure-bundle (6 shards, any 4)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[6.56, "o", "\u2713 sent 'report.txt' \u2014 sealed, notarized, and erasure-bundled\r\n"]
[6.74, "o", "    capture id : ac9a4d16031f3e23ad2e75a4d65eca87\r\n"]
[6.92, "o", "    originator : sensor-7  (device-signed \u2713)\r\n"]
[7.1, "o", "    shards     : 6 (any 4 reconstruct; tolerates losing 2)\r\n"]
[7.28, "o", "    parcel     : parcel.receipt, parcel.bundle, parcel.shard000\u2026parcel.shard005\r\n"]
[7.46, "o", "    \u2192 transport the parcel; receiver runs `etp-custody receive`\r\n"]
[7.64, "o", "\r\n"]
[8.74, "o", "\u001b[1;36m\u25b8 5. Simulate a lossy link: two shards never arrive\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[8.92, "o", "    dropped parcel.shard001 and parcel.shard004 (2 of 6)\r\n"]
[9.1, "o", "\r\n"]
[10.2, "o", "\u001b[1;36m\u25b8 6. inspect the parcel with NO keys \u2014 structural triage before committing\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[10.38, "o", "receipt: parcel.receipt\r\n"]
[10.56, "o", "    capture id : ac9a4d16031f3e23ad2e75a4d65eca87\r\n"]
[10.74, "o", "    originator : sensor-7  (device-signed)\r\n"]
[10.92, "o", "    captured_at: 1782942480.0997832\r\n"]
[11.1, "o", "    operator vk: 0T95ChiKHzT0ARfZu/2nksr9\u2026\r\n"]
[11.28, "o", "    log state  : tree_size=1  STH seq=0  leaf=0\r\n"]
[11.46, "o", "    checks:\r\n"]
[11.64, "o", "      [\u2713] operator STH signature valid\r\n"]
[11.82, "o", "      [\u2713] inclusion proof reconstructs the attested root\r\n"]
[12.0, "o", "      [\u2713] originator (device) signature valid\r\n"]
[12.18, "o", "      [\u2713] shards present: 4/6 valid, need 4\r\n"]
[12.36, "o", "      [\u2713] reassembled blob matches manifest sealed_hash\r\n"]
[12.54, "o", "    \u2192 structurally valid\r\n"]
[12.72, "o", "    (authenticity requires pinning: use `verify --operator/--expect-originator`)\r\n"]
[12.9, "o", "\r\n"]
[14.0, "o", "\u001b[1;36m\u25b8 7. receive: reassemble from survivors + verify (operator & device PINNED) + open\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[14.18, "o", "\u2713 received \u2192 recovered.txt  (62 B)\r\n"]
[14.36, "o", "    reassembled  : from 4 shards (needed 4/6)\r\n"]
[14.54, "o", "    provenance   : VERIFIED \u00b7 operator PINNED \u00b7 device PINNED\r\n"]
[14.72, "o", "    originator   : sensor-7  (device-signed)\r\n"]
[14.9, "o", "    \u2713 recovered plaintext is byte-identical to the original\r\n"]
[15.08, "o", "\r\n"]
[16.18, "o", "\u001b[1;36m\u25b8 8. fail-closed: pin the WRONG device \u2014 provenance fails, nothing is opened\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[16.36, "o", "FAIL \u2014 provenance did NOT verify; refusing to open the payload\r\n"]
[16.54, "o", "    \u2713 refused to open; no plaintext written: none\r\n"]
[16.72, "o", "\r\n"]
[17.82, "o", "\u001b[1;36m\u25b8 9. batch-send a whole directory under ONE append-only log\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[18.0, "o", "\u2713 batch-sent 3 files \u2192 parcels/  (one append-only log, shared STH seq 1, root a5e3ed3000377b3e\u2026)\r\n"]
[18.18, "o", "    each file bundled 5/3; index: parcels/batch.json\r\n"]
[18.36, "o", "\r\n"]
[19.46, "o", "\u001b[1;36m\u25b8 10. audit: prove two receipts belong to one append-only log (no rewrite/fork)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[19.64, "o", "CONSISTENT \u2014 STH seq 1 (size 4) is an append-only extension of seq 0 (size 1)\r\n"]
[19.82, "o", "    the notary did not rewrite or fork history between these two receipts\r\n"]
[20.0, "o", "\r\n"]
[20.18, "o", "\u001b[1;32m\u2713 done \u2014 post-quantum, tamper-evident, delay-tolerant custody, no blockchain.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
